  "definition": "Computer Numerical Control machining — a subtractive process where cutting tools follow programmed paths to remove material from a solid block, achieving repeatable precision."
 },
 {
  "term": "additive manufacturing",
  "definition": "Manufacturing by building a component layer by layer from a 3D CAD model — commonly called 3D printing. No tooling is required and complex internal geometries are possible."
